WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.052
A drug target should not reverse its apparent

00:00:04.052 --> 00:00:07.204
biological meaning each time the tumour context

00:00:07.204 --> 00:00:10.806
changes. SLIT2 and ROBO make that assumption difficult.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.092
In one cancer context a signalling pathway can favour

00:00:21.092 --> 00:00:24.734
tumour growth. In another it may help restrain it.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:36.647
SLIT2 binds ROBO receptors through a broad protein

00:00:36.647 --> 00:00:40.319
interface, shaped by cellular location and associated

00:00:40.319 --> 00:00:40.843
partners.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:51.606
We surveyed patent families from twenty twenty through

00:00:51.606 --> 00:00:54.723
twenty twenty-six, examining the proposed intervention

00:00:54.723 --> 00:00:56.281
and experimental support.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.724
Antibodies, ligand traps and other strategies promise

00:01:05.724 --> 00:01:09.466
different forms of pathway disruption. Not all claims

00:01:09.466 --> 00:01:12.273
demonstrate the same level of enablement.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.788
Patent filings reveal proposed interventions and

00:01:21.788 --> 00:01:25.682
commercial claims, not confirmed clinical benefit. The

00:01:25.682 --> 00:01:29.019
signalling context must be reconstructed separately.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.990
A useful inhibitor must be matched to the tumour

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.137
biology where the pathway is actually driving disease.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.393
A patent landscape becomes scientifically useful when

00:01:49.393 --> 00:01:53.177
its claims are tested against the different roles this

00:01:53.177 --> 00:01:54.438
pathway can play.
